      ],
      "text": "4. Parent education / anticipatory guidance"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
     "spaceBefore": 9,
     "spaceAfter": 9,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Priorities (11–14 y) [BF4‑AD]: social determinants; physical growth and development; emotional well‑being; risk reduction; safety. "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Guidance = given to the youth first, then to the parent/guardian prn."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 36,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 1.8,
     "spaceAfter": 1.8,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Emotional well‑being:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " normalize difficulty but teach youth to "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "seek help when persistently sad/depressed/hopeless/nervous/angry"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "; tell parents the clinician cares about mental health as much as physical, and to raise mood/behavior/substance‑use concerns."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 36,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 1.8,
     "spaceAfter": 1.8,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Sexuality:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " discuss the individual pubertal trajectory; reassure about asym breast development and transient gynecomastia; educate about menarche/menstrual issues; be open and non‑judgmental about sexual orientation and gender identity; anticipate sexual experimentation; frame w.in the youth's cx."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 36,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 1.8,
     "spaceAfter": 1.8,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
